--- a/specs/state.md
+++ b/specs/state.md
@@ -592,6 +592,52 @@
 - Resume boundary
   - Because call frames add new durable lineage and resume keys, resume from pre-`schema_version: "2.1"` state is rejected unless a tested upgrader ships with the same tranche.
 
+## Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)
+
+`RunState.result_persistence_profile` is an optional additive field (schema stays `2.1`).
+Absent means the historical bundle-backed persistence; `to_dict()` then omits the key and
+loading never infers, backfills or upgrades it. The only supported value is
+`derived_pure_replay.v1`; any other value fails closed with a `ValueError` naming the
+profile at `RunState` construction, `StateManager.initialize(..., result_persistence_profile=...)`
+and on load (a failed load leaves `state.json` byte-for-byte unchanged).
+
+Selection happens only when state is created: a successfully compiled `.orc` run
+(`orchestrator run`), a new root made by `orchestrator resume --force-restart`, and a fresh
+non-iterative child call frame whose callee bundle has `provenance.frontend_kind ==
+"workflow_lisp"` (including a fresh retry after a failed predecessor). Existing roots and
+frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees and iteration-owned child frames keep the historical
+profile; a malformed existing frame (no `state` mapping) is rejected with a `ValueError`
+mentioning `existing call-frame state` before anything is written.
+
+Under the profile, a compiler-generated `pure_projection` that is acyclic and visited at most
+once per scope (see `orchestrator.workflow.pure_result_replay.derive_pure_result_replay_index`)
+persists only the value-free completion shell on success:
+
+```json
+{"name": "<presentation_key>", "step_id": "<step_id>", "visit_count": 1,
+ "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0,
+ "outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution", "class": "completed", "retryable": false},
+ "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}
+```
+
+Failed and skipped rows stay full durable rows. Visit, cursor and settlement are single state
+transactions (`begin_eligible_pure_visit`, `reuse_interrupted_eligible_pure_visit`,
+`settle_eligible_pure_success`, `settle_eligible_pure_failure`). Progress per node classifies as
+`unstarted`, `interrupted`, `derived_complete` or `durable_failure_skip`; anything else is
+`progress_witness_invalid`. Eligible nodes write no result bundle, no private lineage
+(`private_artifact_versions`), no checkpoint record and no restore binding.
+
+Resume re-derives the values later work consumes from bound inputs and durable results, in
+memory, without effects or writes. Gaps fail the run before any effect with error type
+`pure_result_replay_unavailable` and `error.context.reason` one of `durable_input_missing`,
+`durable_input_invalid`, `binding_unresolved`, `evaluation_failed`, `output_contract_invalid`,
+`progress_witness_invalid`. A persisted value row, bundle, private-lineage entry, checkpoint
+record or restore binding for an eligible node is a `profile_conflict` raised before the
+prologue. Default resume admits one zero-record case, `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY`
+(`selection_reason` `validated_frame_entry_replay`, no checkpoint id); otherwise the nearest
+noneligible durable boundary decides (`validated_prior_boundary`) or the resume fails closed
+with `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`.
+
 ## State File Schema (example)
 
 The state file (`${RUN_ROOT}/state.json`) is the authoritative record of execution:
